{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01LTqLrH4hMeNMwHmpFJuNHm","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Shared sub-agent contract for differential testing\n2\t\n3\tWorking dir: `/tmp/harvest-work-P2znNt/translated_rust`\n4\t\n5\t## Goal\n6\tWrite Rust integration tests in `tests/` that load BOTH the C `.so` and the\n7\tRust `.so` via `libloading` and compare outputs byte-for-byte through the FFI\n8\tboundary. The C code is ground truth; fix ONLY the Rust source (`src/`) on any\n9\tdivergence — NEVER edit `c_src/` and NEVER edit the C behavior.\n10\t\n11\t## Harness (already exists — DO NOT rewrite)\n12\t- `tests/common/mod.rs` exposes:\n13\t  - `common::libs()` -> `&'static Libs { c: Library, rust: Library }`\n14\t    (already calls `sodium_init()` on both).\n15\t  - `common::Rng` — deterministic xorshift PRNG: `Rng::new(seed)`, `.fill(&mut buf)`,\n16\t    `.vec(len)`, `.range(n)`, `.next_u64()`.\n17\t  - `sympair!(l, b\"symbol_name\", unsafe extern \"C\" fn(...) -> ...)` macro returns\n18\t    `(c_symbol, rust_symbol)` — call both and compare.\n19\t- Each test file MUST start with:\n20\t  ```rust\n21\t  #[macro_use]\n22\t  mod common;   // provides sympair! via #[macro_export] + common::*\n23\t  use common::libs;\n24\t  ```\n25\t  (Actually `sympair!` is `#[macro_export]` so it's crate-global; just `mod common;` + `use common::{libs, Rng};`.)\n26\t\n27\t## Rules\n28\t1. NEVER call Rust functions directly. Always go through `sympair!` loaded symbols.\n29\t2. Get exact C signatures from the headers in\n30\t   `c_src/libsodium/include/sodium/*.h` and the C source in\n31\t   `c_src/libsodium/**/*.c`.\n32\t3. Phase B (valid path): for each meaningful configuration/input-shape, run MANY\n33\t   randomized inputs (fixed seed) and assert BOTH return code AND output buffers\n34\t   match byte-for-byte.\n35\t4. Phase C (error path): construct each invalid input the C rejects (null ptrs,\n36\t   bad lengths, out-of-range values, tampered ciphertext/tag, wrong sizes) and\n37\t   assert BOTH return the SAME error code / sentinel.\n38\t5. Use the lowest-level entry points too, not just convenience wrappers\n39\t   (e.g. `*_detached`, `*_init/_update/_final` streaming APIs, `*_ref10` internals\n40\t   if exported).\n41\t6. Build/run with: `timeout 600 cargo test --release --test <FILE_STEM> 2>&1 | tail -30`\n42\t   (release keeps the loaded cdylib `target/release/liblibsodium.so` fresh).\n43\t   The C .so is at `c_src/build/libsodium.so` (already built).\n44\t7. If you change `src/`, re-run to confirm all tests pass. Fix root causes.\n45\t\n46\t## Deliverables per agent\n47\t- `tests/<FILE_STEM>.rs` with passing Phase B + Phase C tests.\n48\t- `docs/<FILE_STEM>_ERRORS.md`: rows `| # | function | trigger | expected C result |`\n49\t  for every distinct rejection in your family's C source.\n50\t- `docs/<FILE_STEM>_CONFIGS.md`: rows `| # | entry point(s) | configuration (options+shape) | [x] |`\n51\t  for every meaningful config combination, checked off once its test passes.\n52\t- Report: number of tests, pass/fail, any src/ files changed, any divergences found+fixed.\n53\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_014yNKw8Ef6ycv6sURKvJZQY","session_id":"273db57d-0194-450c-88e2-05a6550af9c0","uuid":"5814389b-5868-48e0-a7e4-ebd3efb83d4a","timestamp":"2026-08-05T06:12:53.103Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Diff tests: public-key family"}
