oring note (not a divergence):** My initial poly1305 wrong-key test flipped one key bit and asserted -1. poly1305 clamps the `r` half of the key, so a single-bit flip can land in a clamped bit and reproduce the same tag — C and Rust *agreed* (both returned 0), so this was a too-strict test assertion, not a library divergence. Fixed by using a fresh independent random key (collision ~2^-128). The HMAC `_init` `sodium_misuse()` path (null key with keylen>0) is process-aborting rather than a return-code path, so it's documented as out of scope in `docs/authmac_ERRORS.md`.\n\n**Docs written:** `/tmp/harvest-work-P2znNt/translated_rust/docs/authmac_ERRORS.md` (24 rejection rows + behavior notes) and `/tmp/harvest-work-P2znNt/translated_rust/docs/authmac_CONFIGS.md` (18 config rows, all checked off).","usage":{"total_tokens":52831,"tool_uses":31,"duration_ms":300186},"uuid":"b158a076-0425-4428-bf6e-2ab7d0e35802","session_id":"273db57d-0194-450c-88e2-05a6550af9c0"}
