{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_bdrk_wyqkmhcrt5mh2tpn25v734a4h7onw5kctl454equt5bzz6tshh2q","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. All work complete.\n\n## Report\n\n**Family:** KEM + IPCRYPT (`crypto_kem_mlkem768`, `crypto_kem_xwing`, `crypto_ipcrypt`)\n\n**Tests:** 15, all passing, 0 failed. Run via `timeout 600 cargo test --release --test kemip`.\n\n**src/ changes:** None. The Rust implementation was already byte-for-byte correct against the C ground truth across every config and error path — no divergences found.\n\n**Deliverables:**\n- `/tmp/harvest-work-P2znNt/translated_rust/tests/kemip.rs`\n- `/tmp/harvest-work-P2znNt/translated_rust/docs/kemip_ERRORS.md`\n- `/tmp/harvest-work-P2znNt/translated_rust/docs/kemip_CONFIGS.md`\n\n**Key findings from the C source that shaped the tests:**\n- Both KEMs expose deterministic entry points (`*_seed_keypair`, `*_enc_deterministic`) confirmed exported in both `.so` files, so all KEM comparisons are true byte-for-byte, not just roundtrip. Randomized `keypair`/`enc` just wrap these with `randombytes_buf`.\n- ML-KEM `enc_deterministic` is the only hard-error path: returns `-1` when the pk polyvec is non-canonical (`polyvec_is_canonical`, coeff >= q=3329). Tested with all-`0xFF` pk and 128 random pks (return-code parity per input).\n- X-Wing `enc_deterministic` returns `-1` when its embedded ML-KEM pk (first 1184 of 1216 bytes) is non-canonical.\n- Decapsulation (both KEMs) uses IND-CCA implicit rejection — tampered ciphertext returns `0` with a pseudo-random shared secret (from SHAKE256(z‖ct)), not an error. Verified byte-equal across libs and distinct from the true secret.\n- ipcrypt API is all `void` (no return codes). Covered all four variants (base/nd/ndx/pfx) plus two non-obvious branches: the degenerate-key collision fallback in ndx and pfx (equal key halves → `diff==0` → re-expand from `k[i]^0x5a`), and the pfx IPv4-mapped path (`prefix_start=96`).