ul -1/sentinel paths from `sodium_misuse()`→abort paths) and `docs/sodiumutils_CONFIGS.md` (43 config rows, all checked off).\n\n**Notable design note:** The C `.so` is built with no `HAVE_*` macros (equivalent to `--disable-asm`), so `sodium_runtime_has_*` all return 0 on the portable fallback — matching the Rust hardcoded zeros on this x86_64 host. `sodium_misuse()`→`abort()` paths (e.g. `bin2hex`/`bin2base64` too-small buffer, invalid base64 variant) are intentionally not exercised in-process since aborting would kill the shared test binary; they're documented instead."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":500,"cache_read_input_tokens":94432,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":500,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01Fcu1ExJLM6gmE37shUuTws","session_id":"273db57d-0194-450c-88e2-05a6550af9c0","uuid":"d4113a00-d261-499d-bec5-e51a612371f3","timestamp":"2026-08-05T06:20:02.947Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Diff tests: sodium utils"}
