nces found:** None.\n\n**Notable:** AES-256-GCM `is_available()` returns 0 on both libraries on this host (no hardware AES/PCLMUL/AVX), so the one-shot crypto body — which calls `sodium_misuse()`/`abort()` when unavailable — is skipped; availability parity is still asserted. This is documented in the ERRORS doc (row 9).\n\n**Docs written:** `docs/aead_ERRORS.md` (21 rejection rows) and `docs/aead_CONFIGS.md` (24 config rows, all checked off).","usage":{"total_tokens":83461,"tool_uses":33,"duration_ms":554609},"uuid":"c598b575-3b04-4149-bca2-706be036a064","session_id":"273db57d-0194-450c-88e2-05a6550af9c0"}
